From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 02:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: mediatek-ge-soc: support LED polarity on MT7988

The MT7988 PHY driver derives the polarity of LED0 from the bootstrap
register and hard-codes that of LED1 to what the reference board uses.
Boards that wire the LEDs differently end up with LEDs that are lit
while the port is down and dark while it is up, e.g. the LTC Velo7 Max,
whose green LEDs on LED0 are active high and orange LEDs on LED1 active
low on every port, which the derived polarities get wrong for LAN2's
LED1 and LAN3's LED0.

Implement led_polarity_set() for MT7988. phylib applies the active-low
and active-high properties of the LED nodes after the driver's probe,
so a polarity given in the device tree overrides the derived one, and
boards without these properties keep the current behaviour.

On MT7988, MTK_PHY_LED_ON_POLARITY makes the pin drive high for an LED
that is on: mt7988_phy_led_get_polarity() sets it for an LED0 strapped
to GND, and setting it on the Velo7 Max lights its active-high LEDs.
This is the opposite of what an7581_phy_led_polarity_set() maps the
bit to, so that one cannot be reused.

---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/mediatek/mtk-ge-soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/mediatek/mtk-ge-soc.c
@@ -1298,6 +1298,35 @@ static bool mt7988_phy_led_get_polarity(
 	return false;
 }
 
+/* MTK_PHY_LED_ON_POLARITY makes the LED pin drive high while the LED is on,
+ * as mt7988_phy_led_get_polarity() sets it for the LED0 strapped to GND.
+ */
+static int mt7988_phy_led_polarity_set(struct phy_device *phydev, int index,
+				       unsigned long modes)
+{
+	u16 val = 0;
+	u32 mode;
+
+	if (index >= MTK_PHY_MAX_LEDS)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	for_each_set_bit(mode, &modes, __PHY_LED_MODES_NUM) {
+		switch (mode) {
+		case PHY_LED_ACTIVE_HIGH:
+			val = MTK_PHY_LED_ON_POLARITY;
+			break;
+		case PHY_LED_ACTIVE_LOW:
+			break;
+		default:
+			return -EINVAL;
+		}
+	}
+
+	return phy_modify_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_VEND2, index ?
+			      MTK_PHY_LED1_ON_CTRL : MTK_PHY_LED0_ON_CTRL,
+			      MTK_PHY_LED_ON_POLARITY, val);
+}
+
 static int mt7988_phy_fix_leds_polarities(struct phy_device *phydev)
 {
 	struct pinctrl *pinctrl;
@@ -1504,6 +1533,7 @@ static struct phy_driver mtk_socphy_driv
 		.led_hw_is_supported = mt798x_phy_led_hw_is_supported,
 		.led_hw_control_set = mt798x_phy_led_hw_control_set,
 		.led_hw_control_get = mt798x_phy_led_hw_control_get,
+		.led_polarity_set = mt7988_phy_led_polarity_set,
 	},
 	{
 		PHY_ID_MATCH_EXACT(MTK_GPHY_ID_AN7581),
